{"id":"p2x3","name":"Latest Customer Record","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","input_dir"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A CRM sends changes of customer records every day. The files are stored in <code>input_dir</code> with this layout:</p>\n<pre class=\"exv\">input_dir/\n  dt=&lt;YYYY-MM-DD&gt;/\n    &lt;name&gt;.csv</pre>\n<p>Each file has a header and the columns <code>customer_id</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>city</code>, <code>updated_at</code> (timestamp written as <code>yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss</code>) and <code>deleted</code> (<code>true</code> or <code>false</code>). A customer can appear in many files and many days.</p>\n<p>The <b>latest version</b> of a customer is chosen with these rules, in this order:</p>\n<ol><li>the version from the most recent <code>dt</code> folder wins;</li><li>inside the same folder, the version with the most recent <code>updated_at</code> wins;</li><li>if there is still a tie, the version from the file whose name is the greatest in alphabetical order wins.</li></ol>\n<p>If the latest version of a customer has <code>deleted = true</code>, the customer is removed from the result, even if older versions were not deleted. E-mails must be trimmed and lower-cased.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the latest version of every customer that is not deleted, with the columns <code>customer_id</code> (string), <code>email</code> (string), <code>city</code> (string) and <code>as_of</code> (date, the <code>dt</code> of the chosen version), sorted by <code>customer_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/dt=2026-03-01/a.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc1,A@Mail.com ,Rabat,2026-03-01 09:00:00,false\nc2,b@mail.com,Fes,2026-03-01 10:00:00,false\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/dt=2026-03-02/a.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc1,a@mail.com,Casablanca,2026-03-01 23:00:00,false\nc2,b@mail.com,Fes,2026-03-02 08:00:00,true\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/dt=2026-03-02/b.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc3,c@mail.com,Lome,2026-03-02 12:00:00,false\n</pre><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>customer_id</th><th>email</th><th>city</th><th>as_of</th></tr><tr><td>c1</td><td>a@mail.com</td><td>Casablanca</td><td>2026-03-02</td></tr><tr><td>c3</td><td>c@mail.com</td><td>Lome</td><td>2026-03-02</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"import os\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\nfrom pyspark.sql.window import Window\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, input_dir: str) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return spark.read.option(\"header\", True).csv(input_dir)\n","hints":["La date vient du nom du dossier dt=YYYY-MM-DD : regexp_extract sur input_file_name() ou sur le chemin quand tu lis chaque fichier.","Window.partitionBy('customer_id').orderBy(dt desc, updated_at desc, file desc) puis row_number() == 1, et SEULEMENT après, filtre deleted.","Si tu filtres deleted avant de prendre la dernière version, un client supprimé réapparaît avec une ancienne version."],"summary_fr":"Des mises à jour de clients arrivent dans des dossiers par jour (dt=YYYY-MM-DD). Garder pour chaque client la version la plus récente (date du dossier, puis updated_at, puis nom de fichier), et enlever les clients dont la dernière version est supprimée (deleted = true).","tags":["dossiers par date","row_number","départage","suppression logique"],"minutes":22,"source":"Kata Lab","files":{"root":"input_dir","files":{"dt=2026-03-01/a.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc1,A@Mail.com ,Rabat,2026-03-01 09:00:00,false\nc2,b@mail.com,Fes,2026-03-01 10:00:00,false\n","dt=2026-03-02/a.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc1,a@mail.com,Casablanca,2026-03-01 23:00:00,false\nc2,b@mail.com,Fes,2026-03-02 08:00:00,true\n","dt=2026-03-02/b.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc3,c@mail.com,Lome,2026-03-02 12:00:00,false\n"}},"visible":[{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"dt=2026-03-01/a.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc1,A@Mail.com ,Rabat,2026-03-01 09:00:00,false\nc2,b@mail.com,Fes,2026-03-01 10:00:00,false\n","dt=2026-03-02/a.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc1,a@mail.com,Casablanca,2026-03-01 23:00:00,false\nc2,b@mail.com,Fes,2026-03-02 08:00:00,true\n","dt=2026-03-02/b.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nc3,c@mail.com,Lome,2026-03-02 12:00:00,false\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","email","city","as_of"],"rows":[["c1","a@mail.com","Casablanca","2026-03-02"],["c3","c@mail.com","Lome","2026-03-02"]]}},{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"dt=2026-04-10/x.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nk9,OLD@x.io,Tanger,2026-04-10 10:00:00,false\n","dt=2026-04-10/y.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nk9,new@x.io,Agadir,2026-04-10 10:00:00,FALSE\n","dt=2026-04-09/z.csv":"customer_id,email,city,updated_at,deleted\nk9,zz@x.io,Oujda,2026-04-11 10:00:00,false\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","email","city","as_of"],"rows":[["k9","new@x.io","Agadir","2026-04-10"]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}